On Tue, 06 Mar 2007 20:24:20 +0100, <masquerade808@gmail.com> wrote:

> I've heard mentions in many different places of intentionally avoiding
> fights and decreasing your own level as a strategy. This is a newbie
> question, but what is the advantage of limiting or decreasing your
> level, what classes should do it, and when?

The levels of generated monsters is based on your XL (and also the DL).
The lower your XL, the easier the monsters.

Some monsters (ants) are pretty tough when not properly equiped but quite  
easy with good AC and weapons. So it can be useful to keep your XL around  
6-7 before getting a good armor and such so that you won't encounter  
soldier ants too early.

In the mid-game, and especially after the quest, the effect of low XL is  
less important since anyway you should be able to deal with most things  
(and you need XL 14 for the quest).
In the late game, after recovering the Aùulet, it has been shown that  
lowering your XL is no more an advantage and you should as well go for the  
extra HPs, skill slots, spell damages, ...

The other advantage of low XL is for "protection racket". When you buy  
divine protection from a priest, the cost is proportional to your XL. Get  
to Minetown with XL1 and you can buy 8 times more protection than at XL8...

